Make bctbx_freeaddrinfo() accept NULL, like freeaddrinfo() does.

bctbx_freeaddrinfo() dereferenced res->ai_canonname without checking res.
On Cygwin, getaddrinfo() returns a single v4-mapped entry for a host
without AAAA records, so the Addrinfo sort test frees a NULL tail and
crashes, taking the whole tester down.

diff --git a/src/utils/port.c b/src/utils/port.c
--- a/src/utils/port.c
+++ b/src/utils/port.c
@@ -1882,6 +1882,7 @@
 	struct addrinfo *it;
 	struct addrinfo *previt = NULL;
 	struct addrinfo *beginit = res;
+	if (res == NULL) return;
 	bool_t looking_for_allocated_by_bctbx = (res->ai_canonname == allocated_by_bctbx_magic) ? TRUE : FALSE;
 
 	for (it = res; it != NULL; it = it->ai_next) {
